                        "entry_id": "9cd073da-f1b3-3d9b-8609-272e6bb7af43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière conforme à la logique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8187b3e0-0d23-45e3-bd16-37b8d78f0fb1",
                                "sense_id": "e6e9f8ff-9199-3dcf-81e7-15726511e323",
                                "text": "Raisonner logiquement'"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c398136a-eb3c-3a44-922e-e4f3ce050879",
                        "entry_id": "9cd073da-f1b3-3d9b-8609-272e6bb7af43",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Par ce qui en découle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "166212b9-5525-4835-ba62-1f0801b7c2fe",
                                "sense_id": "c398136a-eb3c-3a44-922e-e4f3ce050879",
                                "text": "Les doctrines hindouistes traditionnelles, telles qu'elles apparaissent déjà dans les textes sacrés les plus anciens (Rig-Véda, Oupanishad, Pouranas), postulent une division des humains selon une hiérarchie de quatre niveaux, nommés « couleur » (varna). Les deux groupes sociaux dominants (prêtres et guerriers) s'y réservent logiquement la meilleure part."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b3e5f15-a3fb-4377-b94c-b34ecb8678e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cd073da-f1b3-3d9b-8609-272e6bb7af43",
                        "target_lang_word": "logically",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "logically",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9da93513-4dac-32cf-a85b-c225b7fb2b34",
                                        "entry_id": "b0b534c4-b750-3270-8d19-35875225d38d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a logical manner, with logic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b71a1b5-c995-41e4-b826-d2a72afc97bf",
                                                "sense_id": "9da93513-4dac-32cf-a85b-c225b7fb2b34",
                                                "text": "A world, then, is a state of affairs W of this sort: For every state of affairs p, either W logically implies p or W logically implies the negation of p, and there is no state of affairs q such that W logically implies both q and the negation of q."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
